      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 809789940,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I have found in the pipeline job log that it says:\n```\nERROR: Please edit your merge request and make sure the setting\n    ✅ Allow commits from members who can merge to the target branch\nis checked so that maintainers can rebase your change and make minor edits.\n```\nHowever that option is disabled due to project being a private project. When I go to the project, it is indeed set as private but it won't let me change it, and the `Internal` and `Public` options are disabled. How can I set the project visibility to `Public`?",
          "author": {
            "id": 10615678,
            "username": "QuentinArmitage",
            "public_email": null,
            "name": "Patrick Armitage",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
